  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Conjecture on the present",
   "texto": [
    "Para describir un estado presente, los adjetivos usan **-(으)ㄴ 것 같아요**: 피곤하다 → **피곤한 것 같아요** (parece/creo que está cansado), 비싸다 → **비싼 것 같아요**. The verbs use **-는 것 같아요**: ∞ - → **자는 것 같아요** (it seems to sleep). **것 같아요** expresses an impression or evaluation; it can be based on what you see, or other information."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Temporary contrast",
   "texto": [
    "For a conjecture on a past state is used **-았/었던 것 같아요**: For a past action are possible forms like **잤던 것 같아요** (I think he slept); past forms may vary according to aspect and context. For a future or unrealized possibility **-(으)ㄹ 것 같아요** is used, as in the previous lesson. Here we focus on the present / past / basic future contrast."
   ]
